\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Test-set comparison (calibrated). VX: VX-One at three sizes. FPR@95 is FPR@95\%TPR. Vendor rows are single-seed; baseline rows now carry three seeds (42/43/44): seed $\sigma $ of the gate AUROC is $\le $0.0013 on UNSW and EMBER, 0.017--0.027 on by-day CIC (XGBoost 0.637$\pm $0.027), and 0 on saturated CIC --- with three seeds, MLP's UNSW mean (0.9835$\pm $0.0013) statistically ties VX (0.9834, single seed inside MLP's range), so the in-distribution UNSW gate comparison is a tie, not a win (bootstrap 95\% CIs, $B{=}500$: UNSW VX $[0.9828,0.9841]$ vs MLP $[0.9816,0.9828]$ at seed 42). $^{\dagger }$ = under temporal drift (its by-day macro-F1 column is seed-unstable: VX spread 0.24--0.45 across three seeds, and XGBoost's 0.8336 is a single-seed value on the same unstable metric --- Section\nonbreakingspace \ref {sec:e1}); $^{b}$ = detection plateau of saturation (all models $\approx $ 1.0). Full per-dataset table, including ECE columns and Kitsune/RF/MLP rows, in the released results.}}{4}{table.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:e1}{{1}{4}{Test-set comparison (calibrated). VX: VX-One at three sizes. FPR@95 is FPR@95\%TPR. Vendor rows are single-seed; baseline rows now carry three seeds (42/43/44): seed $\sigma $ of the gate AUROC is $\le $0.0013 on UNSW and EMBER, 0.017--0.027 on by-day CIC (XGBoost 0.637$\pm $0.027), and 0 on saturated CIC --- with three seeds, MLP's UNSW mean (0.9835$\pm $0.0013) statistically ties VX (0.9834, single seed inside MLP's range), so the in-distribution UNSW gate comparison is a tie, not a win (bootstrap 95\% CIs, $B{=}500$: UNSW VX $[0.9828,0.9841]$ vs MLP $[0.9816,0.9828]$ at seed 42). $^{\dagger }$ = under temporal drift (its by-day macro-F1 column is seed-unstable: VX spread 0.24--0.45 across three seeds, and XGBoost's 0.8336 is a single-seed value on the same unstable metric --- Section~\ref {sec:e1}); $^{b}$ = detection plateau of saturation (all models $\approx $ 1.0). Full per-dataset table, including ECE columns and Kitsune/RF/MLP rows, in the released results}{table.caption.22}{}}
